  "report_period": "Week 38 (12th Sep to 19th Sep 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Kamsarmax \"TR Lady\" 81/2017 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 01/2027, Rotor sails fitted) was committed to Greek interests at rgn USD 24 mill. Remind you that in August, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Darya Shanti\" 82/2016 Jiangsu, China (SS 02/2026, DD 04/2028, Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 22,3 mill. In addition, clients of POLSTEAM committed the \"Rysy\" 79/2011 New Century, China (SS/DD 03/2026) to undisclosed interests at high USD 11 mill. Note that a couple of weeks ago, the one-year-older \"Adam I\" 79/2010 Fujian, China (SS 06/2030, DD 03/2028, Ice Class II) was committed at USD 11,3 mill. Caravel Group have committed their Ultramax \"Explorer Europe\" 61/2012 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 11/2025) to Chinese interests at rgn USD 18 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"El Comino\" 61/2012 Iwagi, Japan (SS 08/2027, DD 09/2025) was sold back in April at mid USD 19 mill. The Handysize \"Vega Everest\" 35/2011 Nantong, China (SS/DD 11/2026) of Vega Bulk Shipowning was committed to Turkish interests at USD 9,5 mill. Remind you that the \"Yuka D\" 34/2011 Zhejiang, China (SS/DD 01/2026) was sold back in July at USD 9 mill.",
    "tankers": "Formosa Plastics Marine Corp have committed their VLCC \"FPMC C Knight\" 301/2011 IHI, Japan (SS/DD 02/2026, Scrubber fitted) to Greek interests at USD 55 mill. For reference, the one-year-older \"Hakone\" & \"Hakata\" 302/2010 Universal, Japan (SS/DD 11/2025 & SS 03/2030, DD 06/2028, Scrubber fitted) were sold back in May at USD 60 mill each. The Suezmax \"Jag Lok\" 158/2005 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS 06/2028, DD 06/2026, Scrubber fitted, Ice Class 1B) of Great Eastern Shipping was committed to Chinese interests at USD 25,5 mill, while the \"Kriti Vigor\" 159/2005 Hyundai, Korea (SS 02/2030, DD 05/2028, Scrubber fitted) was committed a week ago at USD 29 mill. Vitol International Shipping committed the MR2 \"Elandra Corallo\" 50/2008 Spp, Korea (SS 10/2028, DD 12/2026) to clients of Ancora Investment Trust at xs USD 17 mill. For comparison, the sister vessel \"Valrossa\" 50/2008 Spp, Korea (SS 03/2028, DD 05/2026) was sold back in July at 17 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 12,000/14,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 13,000/15,000 pd range. Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. South East Asian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 17,000/18,000 pd. India trips into China were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. India trips via South Africa into India were fixed around usd 14,000/17,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into India were reported at the level of usd 28,000/30,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 27,000/29,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 17,000/19,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 700K/900K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 15,750 pd for 8/10 months employment basis delivery China. Also, a Kamsarmax was fixed on a period at the usd 22,800 pd basis delivery Continent for 4/6 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "Trips from Philippines into China with nickel ore were reported at the level of usd 15,000/16,000 pd. A number of Indonesian into India were reported fixed in the usd 15,000/17,000 pd range. Arabian Gulf trips into East Coast India were reported at the level of usd 14,000/15,000 pd. West African trips into Continent with bauxite were fixed around usd 17,000/19,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Arabian Gulf trips into West Coast India were reported at the level of usd 12,000/13,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips via South Africa into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 11,000/13,000 pd. West African trips via South America into South Africa were reported at the level of usd 15,000/16,000 pd. Continental trips via Baltic into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 17,000/18,000 pd. South American trips into US Gulf or Caribs were reported at the level of usd 21,000/22,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into West Coast South America were fixed around usd 22,000/23,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
